  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">U.S.-Mexico Grassland Bird Conservation, Phase XI PP</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will 1) expand our work with landowners in Chihuahua to improve habitat using guidance from the Chihuahuan Desert Wintering Grassland Bird Conservation Plan and reduce threats to Spragues Pipits and up to 27 other high-priority grassland birds on at least 15,000 ha (possibly up to 24,000 ha), 2) advance research on factors limiting Bairds Sparrow and Grasshopper Sparrow survival in Chihuahua and explore possibilities for expanding this research.to Spragues Pipit, and 3) develop decision support tools and BMPs for at least 7 high-priority grassland bird species breeding on Colorado State Trust Lands to improve habitat management and reduce threats from oil and gas development for up to 20 high-priority grassland bird species on roughly 2 million acres in eastern Colorado.</narrative>
  </description>
